<title>USA: Oct same-store retail spending rose - TeleCheck.</title>
<headline>Oct same-store retail spending rose - TeleCheck.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>October same-store retail spending rose 1.2 percent over the same period last year, TeleCheck Services Inc said.</p>
<p>&quot;October's same-store gain is consistent with the slowing pace of the economy and is an improvement from September's 1.5 percent drop,&quot; said William Ford, TeleCheck's senior economic advisor.  </p>
<p>Despite October's moderate pace, Ford said the company expects a two to four percent same-store sales gain during the holiday shopping period because &quot;consumer confidence is strong and the employment picture is good.&quot;</p>
